.TH XRDTOKEN 1 "2026" "XRootD" "XRootD Commands"
.SH NAME
xrdtoken \- request storage macaroons and OAuth access tokens
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xrdtoken macaroon
[\fB--write\fR] [\fB--validity\fR \fIminutes\fR]
[\fB--activity\fR \fIname\fR] \fIhttps-or-davs-url\fR
.br
.B xrdtoken oauth
\fB--issuer\fR \fIurl\fR \fB--scope\fR \fIscope\fR
\fB--client-id\fR \fIid\fR
.br
.B xrdtoken id
\fB--issuer\fR \fIurl\fR \fB--scope\fR \fIopenid-scope\fR
\fB--client-id\fR \fIid\fR
[\fB--device-endpoint\fR \fIurl\fR \fB--token-endpoint\fR \fIurl\fR]
.br
.B xrdtoken oauth-device
\fB--issuer\fR \fIurl\fR \fB--scope\fR \fIscope\fR
\fB--client-id\fR \fIid\fR
[\fB--device-endpoint\fR \fIurl\fR \fB--token-endpoint\fR \fIurl\fR]
.br
.B xrdtoken oauth-macaroon
\fB--issuer\fR \fIurl\fR [\fB--client-id\fR \fIid\fR]
[\fB--write\fR] [\fB--validity\fR \fIminutes\fR]
[\fB--activity\fR \fIname\fR] \fIhttps-or-davs-url\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a token to standard output. Direct macaroon requests POST to the storage
URL. OAuth requests use issuer discovery. The \fBoauth\fR and
\fBoauth-macaroon\fR forms use the client credentials grant. They can
authenticate with a client certificate or the
\fBXRD_TOKEN_CLIENT_SECRET\fR environment variable. The \fBid\fR and
\fBoauth-device\fR forms use device authorization and print a verification
URL and code to standard error. They output only the requested token after
authorization completes.
For providers that do not advertise device authorization metadata, pass
both endpoint options explicitly. The endpoints must use HTTPS.
The \fBoauth-macaroon\fR form derives activity scopes from the storage path.
Issuer discovery tries RFC 8414 metadata and then OpenID Connect metadata.
An issuer failure does not change the requested token type.
Use \fB--timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR to set the deadline for each request
workflow; the default uses the client timeout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XRD_TOKEN_CLIENT_SECRET
Optional client secret for OAuth. Keep it out of command arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xrdfs (1),
.BR xrdcp (1)
